# "Whenever YOU sacrifice a token": Bot1 has the Sackville-Bagginses; on turn 2 Bot2 casts Thraben Inspector and later sacrifices its
# own Clue ({2}) on turn 4. That is Bot2's sacrifice, not Bot1's: nobody loses life from it (Bot1 stays at 20, Bot2 at 20).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
The Sackville-Bagginses
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Thraben Inspector
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Sackville-Bagginses.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Clue Token.Activate
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Plains; Thraben Inspector
